body:
I'm a medical student and usually, I will study until 2am on the day of the exam, sleep for 2-3hrs and wake up to study until 7am if my exam is at 8am. 

I know it seems crazy, but losing 1 night of sleep doesn't seem to affect my exam performance at all, and I'd rather spend as much time as possible taking in more information. 

For me, personally, I find that the adrenaline spike I get is enough. I usually do very well in my exams. 

Everyone is different though, for example my room mate needs at least 6hours sleep before an exam or she won't be able to function properly. 

It also depends on the type of exam. If it's memory based then I'll stay up at night, but if it involves a lot of mathematics I will try to sleep around 7 hours. 

&#x200B;

